1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
'Cause I…

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
I can't see him

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,000
as just something to exterminate now.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,000
You heard him.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:23,000
[moans]

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,000
So why would we keep doing this?

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
I can't think of a reason.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,000
[Knov] The King.

9
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,000
The soldiers are of no consequence.

10
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,000
The King can just wave his hand

11
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,000
and turn all of them into evil spawn.

12
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,000
[opening theme music playing]

13
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:20,000
[singer singing in English]

14
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

15
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,000
[singer singing in English]

16
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

17
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
POSE X AND X NAME

18
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Why do you and I have to fight?

19
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,000
Huh?

20
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:44,000
[King] You have absolutely
no chance of defeating me.

21
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,000
There is no need for us
to hasten your inevitable death.

22
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
[wind blowing]

23
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:56,000
Saying I can't win
is pretty presumptuous of you.

24
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:00,000
I can tell that you don't know
squat about me.

25
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,000
[blows]

26
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,000
If you judge a book by its cover,

27
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,000
don't be surprised if you get burned.

28
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
You don't seem like some ordinary man

29
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,000
who can't read the state of the battle.

30
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:27,000
Originally, you pathetic humans
were no more than livestock to me,

31
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:37,000
I have since determined
that there are a few humans

32
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
that are worth keeping alive.

33
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Like that girl, for example.

34
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:50,000
You are worthy as well. I can sense it.

35
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,000
If you will back down this instant…

36
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:58,000
then I will consider sparing you.

37
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,000
[Netero] You're saying you would spare me
and not the others?

38
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:08,000
Is that right?

39
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Given my unique position,

40
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:18,000
I simply can't accept that offer.

41
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:24,000
[suspense music playing]

42
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:30,000
[narrator] Meanwhile,
deep within the palace,

43
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:34,000
in exchange for his agreement
to stay still for the moment,

44
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:42,000
[sinister music playing]

45
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:03,000
and all that had transpired
since they had separated.

46
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:12,000
to ensure that Gon's attention
would be focused

47
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,000
on the explanation.

48
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:20,000
But Pitou, unable to describe
the events accurately,

49
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:38,000
There was no significant change in Gon.

50
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:40,000
[imperceptible]

51
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:54,000
The King…

52
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:59,000
he left with the enemy
of his own volition

53
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,000
by that doorway.

54
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:04,000
There's no need for us to go after him.

55
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,000
[Shaiapouf] Hmm.

56
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,000
I understand.

57
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,000
He went south.

58
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:15,000
Thank you for telling me.

59
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,000
A fine play, Pitou.

60
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:24,000
Then we should stay here
and await his return.

61
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,000
We must be patient.

62
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,000
The other segments will go…

63
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:47,000
to the King!

64
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:06,000
You will fight
knowing that you cannot win?

65
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,000
children may starve to death,

66
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,000
while on the left,

67
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:39,000
idle dregs who do nothing
have everything they need.

68
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,000
[Netero] Hmm.

69
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,000
[King] I don't deny that I'll start

70
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:16,000
by using power and terror
to accomplish my objective,

71
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,000
You see, I have learned

72
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:27,000
what true power is meant to be used for…

73
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,000
[imperceptible]

74
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,000
[King] …to protect the weak
who deserve to live.

75
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
That is its purpose.

76
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:41,000
Power shouldn't be used
to torment the defeated.

77
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,000
[suspense music playing]

78
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:21,000
yet it seems he hasn't yet realized

79
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:45,000
[somber music playing]

80
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,000
[man] We're counting on you.

81
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:50,000
You have only one mission to carry out,

82
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:54,000
the immediate execution of all
of these dangerous creatures.

83
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:04,000
Will that be acceptable to you?

84
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:07,000
Well, don't ask me.

85
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:10,000
We wouldn't dream of telling
the experts how to proceed.

86
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:22,000
Yes, of course. I understand.

87
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,000
Look, King…

88
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:53,000
we've all got problems, you know.

89
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,000
[gasps]

90
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:02,000
[ominous music playing]

91
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:32,000
[wind blowing]

92
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:37,000
[wings fluttering]

93
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,000
[gasps]

94
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:50,000
[Menthuthuyoupi] I can't sense
anyone else fighting here.

95
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:53,000
Does that mean
that I'm the only one left?

96
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:56,000
[Shaiapouf] Youpi!

97
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:57,000
[Menthuthuyoupi] Huh? Huh?

98
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,000
If I moved all my particles at once,

99
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:18,000
it would have been suspicious,
so I moved slowly.

100
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:22,000
I'm sure you're rushed,

101
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:23,000
but could you spare a moment?

102
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Yeah. I suppose I've got a minute.

103
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:35,000
Guess everyone
does have their reasons.

104
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:36,000
[Shaiapouf] Uh…

105
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:41,000
You sound so grown up.

106
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:54,000
I hope Pitou's change
will benefit the King.

107
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:58,000
But I can't be sure.

108
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:01,000
I've no conclusive proof
one way or the other.

109
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:06,000
[sentimental music playing]

110
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:14,000
[narrator] Based on his own experiences,

111
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:17,000
Youpi could understand Pitou's behavior.

112
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:19,000
-[Shaiapouf] Youpi.
-[Menthuthuyoupi] Huh?

113
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
So tell me.

114
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:24,000
What do you think we should do now?

115
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
[narrator] He was being tested.

116
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:37,000
This tactic made it quite clear to Youpi

117
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:41,000
that Pouf was afraid,
unnerved by the subtle changes

118
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:07,000
[suspense music playing]

119
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,000
[Menthuthuyoupi]
There's no time to waste.

120
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,000
We must go to the King…

121
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:25,000
Indeed, you are.

122
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:28,000
[narrator] Only one thing
concerned him at the moment,

123
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:31,000
and that was leaving
as quickly as possible…

124
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:36,000
because the fear that gripped Pouf

125
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:39,000
had taken hold of Youpi as well.

126
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:51,000
[suspense music playing]

127
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,000
[spits]

128
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:20,000
[Netero] I'm sure that was a direct hit.

129
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:28,000
[King] A very good attack.

130
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,000
I wasn't expecting it.

131
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:35,000
[wind blowing]

132
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Are you satisfied?

133
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:18,000
[Netero] Third hand!

134
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:30,000
I cannot back down any longer.

135
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,000
[gasps]

136
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:40,000
[creaking]

137
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:43,000
[ominous music playing]

138
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:58,000
[narrator] From the King's perspective,

139
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,000
the wrath that was unleashed
was unimpressive,

140
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:03,000
seemingly no stronger
than that of a child

141
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:04,000
throwing a tantrum.

142
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:09,000
But the King's full power
was violent enough

143
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:11,000
to make Netero jump back

144
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:13,000
more than twice his usual distance.

145
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:20,000
Netero couldn't help but feel insulted
by this turn of events

146
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:23,000
and by the fact that his determination,
strong as it was,

147
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:50,000
If it were that simple,
I wouldn't have to do this.

148
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,000
Wait.

149
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:02,000
Exchanging words?

150
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:18,000
How is it that you have come
into possession of my name?

151
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:50,000
Are you interested in fighting me now?

152
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:56,000
I'll make you a deal.

153
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:58,000
If you can force me to admit defeat,

154
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:15,000
So I'll be playing
without a rook and bishop.

155
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:17,000
[suspense music playing]

156
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:55,000
[suspense music playing]

157
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:13,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

158
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:33,000
[Gon] Next time,
"Centipede and Memory."

159
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:35,000
What do you want to be
in your next life?

160
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:37,000
[Killua] Uh, you first.

161
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:40,000
[Gon] In my next life, I wanna be me
so I can meet you again!

162
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:46,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
